From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:41:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] feat(linux): extension popups, network rules and
 add-ons from the stores

- Popups open inside the browser window, as a view on the stage's layer
  above the tab pages and under their button, rendered in software, sized
  to their page as Chrome sizes them, and closed by Escape or when focus
  leaves. A popup's "current window" is the browser window it came from.
- Content-script CSS from the manifest goes in at document_start.
- Tab and window events: the differences between two of the shell's
  snapshots of windows and tabs.
- declarativeNetRequest: enabled static rulesets, dynamic and session
  rules compile into one WebKit content-blocker list on every tab of the
  profile; rules WebKit cannot express are left out.
- scripting.registerContentScripts and its siblings.
- The Chrome Web Store's in-page button, as on macOS, in a script world of
  its own.
- addons.mozilla.org's "Download Firefox" button becomes "Add to
  Zephium"; a .xpi from the store is fetched and offered for the same
  review as a dropped file.
- Extensions never script the add-on stores.
- API members extensions use at start answer instead of being undefined.
